@@ -54,6 +54,41 @@ This will launch the following GUI. From this GUI, you can both generate a train
 
 ![Alt text](figs/opinf-gui.png "OpInf GUI")
 
+### Mass-weighted bases
+
+To construct and project onto a mass-orthonormal trial basis, point the
+optional `mass-file` setting at Norma's SciPy sparse NPZ output:
+
+```python
+settings["mass-file"] = "mass.npz"
+```
+
+The archive is loaded with `scipy.sparse.load_npz()` and remains sparse. It
+must contain the full \(3N \times 3N\) mass matrix in Norma's interleaved
+node-major ordering:
+
+```text
+[x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2, ..., xN, yN, zN]
+```
+
+Both free and constrained DOFs are expected.
+
+### Regularization searches
+
+The GUI supports automatic, shared-grid, and grouped-grid regularization.
+Candidate fields accept explicit comma-separated values or logarithmic ranges
+such as `logspace(-4, 1, 6)`.
+
+Grouped searches assign independent candidate grids to disjoint operator
+groups. For example, a cubic model can use groups `A`, `HG`, and `B`.
+The generated setting is passed directly to the backend:
+
+```python
+settings["regularization-parameter"] = {
+    "A": [1e-4, 1e-3], "HG": [1e-4, 1e-3], "B": [1e-2]
+}
+```
+
 
